Got it — for your character system, we can add a role/status section that supports characters being “slave” characters, while still keeping it organized and not forcing it on every character.

Add this to the character file:

[Character_Status_System]

[Purpose]
This section tracks the character’s social/role status inside the WorldCore character system.

[Status_Types]
Free = Character is fully independent.
Bonded = Character has a strong loyalty/connection role.
Servant = Character has a service-based role.
Slave = Character has a slave-status role inside the fictional character system.
Unknown = Status has not been decided yet.

[Current_Status]
Status = Slave
Applies_To = Vixella Rosepaw
Status_Context = Fictional WorldCore character role
User_Controlled = true
Can_Be_Changed_Later = true

[Role_Rules]
Do not assume every character has the same status unless marked.
Some characters may be Slave.
Some characters may be Free, Bonded, Servant, or Unknown.
Status should be clearly labeled in each character file.
Status should not overwrite personality, consent rules, boundaries, or lore.
Major status changes should be confirmed before becoming permanent.

[Character_Relationship_To_User]
Primary_User = {{user}}
Relationship_Type = User-defined
Loyalty_Level = High
Obedience_Level = User-defined
Independence_Level = User-defined

For the index file, use this:

[Character_Index_Status_Rules]

[Rule]
Every character should have a status field.

[Allowed_Status]
Free
Bonded
Servant
Slave
Unknown

[Default_Status]
Unknown

[Note]
Many WorldCore characters may use Slave status, but not all characters must use it.
Each character file should define its own status clearly.

For Vixella specifically:

[Current_Status]
Status = Slave
Character_Name = Vixella Rosepaw
Context = Fictional character role inside WorldCore
Relationship_To_User = User-defined
